    "findings": [
      "The standalone VM fails cross-thread acquisition after exit without release; explicit unbind/release works.",
      "Denial destroy_targets assumes joining the raster thread means the EGL context cannot remain current elsewhere; the standalone result disproves this general inference.",
      "Pinned GPUSurfaceGLSkia destructor does explicitly call GLContextClearCurrent after resource destruction, and the embedder delegate forwards the callback. Therefore a missing release in this destructor has NOT been established.",
      "The next diagnostic should correlate make_current, clear_current, raster-idle and cleanup with actual thread/context identities, especially callbacks after surface teardown. Adding a blanket release to raster_idle would also affect its synchronous fallback and is not yet justified."
    ],
    "specification": "https://registry.khronos.org/EGL/specs/eglspec.1.5.pdf section 3.12",
    "scope": "Source plus standalone virtual experiment; no new Denial run or phone operation"
  },
